  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153327/assets/171e55cb16b67bba62ca0a1e85c54ca2cb8fc10e8284b9ca7fdcf9ddd3862502.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the square above?",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(2\\,\\text{m})^{2} \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{m}\\times 2\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =(2\\times 2)\\times (\\text{m}\\times \\text{m}) \\\\  & =4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
